# Everything here is either rebuilt inside the image or has no business in the build
# context. A smaller context is a faster build: Docker ships the whole thing to the
# daemon before the first instruction runs.

# Installed by `npm ci` in the web stage. Tens of megabytes, and platform-specific
# binaries (esbuild ships one per OS and arch) that would be wrong for the container.
web/node_modules/

# Built by the web stage. Excluding it also guarantees the image cannot accidentally
# ship a stale bundle from the host instead of the one it just built.
web/dist/

# History, editor and OS noise.
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store

# Documentation and screenshots. docs/branding is deliberately NOT excluded: the
# frontend imports the wordmark from there, so the web stage needs it.
docs/screenshots/
*.md
LICENSE
